Aristotle's views on all scientific matters, including psychology, were accepted.
As Greek knowledge declined, the West severed its connection with the scientific and philosophical roots of ancient Greece.
Many regard physiological and behavioral rhythms, usually as closely associated with circadian cycles and their generation, as biological clocks.
Circadian rhythms, which are not merely responses to external periodic cues, have been documented in most living organisms, including bacteria, fungi, plants, and animals.
Biological clocks are self-sustaining oscillators that maintain a periodic cycle of a free-running rhythm in the absence of external cues.
The Hershey-Chase experiment was one of the most compelling pieces of evidence for the genetic nature of DNA.
"Hershey" and "Chase" used phages or viruses to insert their DNA into bacteria.
They conducted two experiments in which they labeled the DNA in the phage with radioactive phosphorus or the phage protein with radioactive sulfur.
A mutation can have very different effects, depending on the type of mutation, the importance of the genetic segment affected, and whether the affected cells are germ line cells or not.
Only mutations in microbial-like cells can be passed on to children, whereas mutations in other locations may cause cell death or cancer.
Ecotourism focuses on attracting individuals interested in visiting natural areas, with the aim of enjoying landscapes such as plants and wildlife.
Examples of activities at this site include hunting, fishing, photography, birdwatching, visiting parks, and studying information about the ecosystem.
A sample of that visit, photography, and learning about organogatoangz in Borneo
Every morning, people from small towns in the county leave by car to go to their workplaces and are then transferred by others whose destination is the same place they came from.
In this dynamic transportation shuttle, everyone is connected to and supported by a personal car-based transportation system in some way.
Now science shows that this carbon-based economy has taken the biosphere out of one of its stable states, a condition that has supported and sustained human evolution over the past two million years.
Everyone in the community participates and uses transportation systems. Almost everyone complains about the transportation system.
In developed countries, you rarely hear about complaints at the same level regarding water quality or bridge collapses.
Why have transportation systems caused such complaints, why do we witness their failure every day? Is this due to the inefficiency of vehicle engineers? Or is there a more fundamental reason?
Traffic flow is the study of the movement of individual drivers and vehicles between two points and their interaction with each other.
Unfortunately, studying traffic flow is difficult, because driver behavior cannot be predicted with 100% certainty.
Fortunately, drivers tend to behave within a suitable and logical range; therefore, traffic flows tend to have a logical structure, which can be approximately specified mathematically.
To better illustrate traffic flow, relationships among the three defined characteristics have been established: 1) flow, 2) density, and 3) speed.
These relationships assist in the planning, design, and operation of highway facilities.
Insects were the first group of animals to go into the air. Their ability to fly helped them escape predators more easily and enabled them to find food and mates more effectively.
Most insects have the ability to fold their wings back along the length of their bodies behind the back.
This ability gives them the opportunity to hide from hunters across a wider range of smaller spaces.
Today, the only insects that cannot fold their wings behind their backs are midges and one-day mosquitoes.
Thousands of years ago, a man named Aristarchus said that the solar system revolves around the Sun.
Some thought he was right, but many people held a different belief; that the solar system, including the Sun (and even other stars), revolves around the Earth.
This seems logical, because on Earth you don't feel that you are moving, right?
The Amazon River is the second longest river in the world and the largest river by volume. The amount of water carried by this river is eight times greater than that of the world's second largest river.
The Amazon is also the widest river on Earth, and in some places its width reaches six miles.
Twenty percent of the freshwater that flows from the world's rivers into the oceans comes from the Amazon River.
The main stem of the Amazon River is 6,387 kilometers (3,980 miles) long and collects water from thousands of small rivers.
Although the construction of stone pyramids continued until the end of the Old Kingdom, no pyramid ever surpassed the pyramids of Giza in size and technical superiority in construction.
The ancient Egyptians were amazed to see the historical structures of their ancestors, which dated back more than a thousand years.
The population of Vatican City is about 800 people. It is the smallest independent country in the world and also has the smallest population among countries.
The Vatican City uses Italian as its language in legislative and administrative communications.
Italian is also a commonly used language by most people working in this state, while Latin is frequently used in religious ceremonies.
All citizens of Vatican City are Roman Catholics.
People have known basic chemical elements such as gold, silver, and copper since ancient times, because all these elements can be found in pure form in nature and their extraction using relatively simple primitive tools is feasible.
Aristotle, the philosopher, established a hypothesis based on the idea that everything is composed of a combination of one or more of four elements. These elements were earth, water, air, and fire.
It was more similar to four states of matter (in the same order): solid, liquid, gas, and plasma, although he also proposed the theory that they transform into new forms of matter, which constitute what we observe.
Alloys are essentially combinations of two or more metals. Remember that many elements exist in the periodic table.
Elements such as calcium and potassium are considered metals. Of course, metals such as silver and gold also exist.
There are also alloys that contain certain amounts of non-metallic elements such as carbon.
Everything in this world is made of matter. All matter is composed of tiny particles called atoms.
Atoms are so incredibly small that trillions of them can fit in the period at the end of this sentence.
