Winter sports on snow, such as skiing and snowboarding, are popular activities in which, using ski poles or a snowboard attached to your feet, you glide down snowy, sloped terrain.
Skiing is the main activity of the trip, which has a large number of enthusiasts and is occasionally known as "ski tourism," meaning the planning of a whole vacation around skiing at a specific location.
Skiing is a very ancient idea—paintings in caves depicting skiers date back to 5000 BC.
Skiing on hills dates back at least to the 17th century, and in 1861, Norwegians in Australia opened the first ski recreational club.
Ski touring: This activity is also called ski touring in remote areas, ski tour, or ski trekking.
