Europe is a relatively small continent, yet it has a large number of independent countries. Under normal circumstances, traveling between numerous countries requires undergoing visa application procedures and passport controls multiple times.
Nevertheless, the Schengen area functions like a country in this respect.
As long as you reside in this area, you can generally cross the borders without having to go through passport control again.
Similarly, with a Schengen visa, there is no longer a need to apply for a visa separately for each of the Schengen member countries, thus saving you time, money, and paperwork.
