Harsh weather conditions refer to a general term for dangerous weather phenomena that may cause damage, disrupt social life, or result in loss of human lives.
Dry weather can occur anywhere in the world, and there are various types of it, which may depend on geography, topography, and weather conditions.
Strong winds, hail, excessive rainfall, fires, as well as lightning, thunderstorms, waterfalls, and seasonal storms are all forms and effects of severe weather.
Regional and seasonal extreme weather phenomena include blizzards, snowstorms, ice storms, and dust storms.
Travelers are strongly advised to remain aware of any potential severe weather conditions affecting their area, as these conditions may impact travel plans.
