Breaking waves are the backwash currents of waves that move from the shore toward the sea, which usually occur at cliffs or similar locations.
The return flow is concentrated due to the underwater topography in several deeper sections, and a rapid current toward deeper water may occur there.
Most deaths occur due to exhaustion from struggling to swim against the wave's current, which can be impossible.
As soon as you leave the current, returning by swimming will not be any harder than normal conditions.
