The capital of Moldova is Chișinău. The local language is Romanian, but Russian is widely used there.
Moldova is a multi-ethnic republic suffering from ethnic and tribal conflicts.
In 1994, this dispute led to the establishment of the self-declared republic of "Transnistria" in eastern Moldova, which has its own government and currency, but is not recognized officially by any member states of the United Nations.
Despite the failure of political negotiations, economic relations between the two parts of Moldova have been reestablished.
The main religion of the people of Moldova is Eastern Orthodox Christianity.
İzmir is Turkey's third largest city and the country's second largest port after Istanbul, with a population of approximately 3.7 million people, and it is considered one of the country's most important transportation hubs.
