Christmas is one of the most important holidays in Christianity and is celebrated as the anniversary of the birth of Jesus Christ.
Many of the traditions of these holidays have also been adopted by people in Christian countries who do not adhere to this religion, as well as by non-Christians around the world.
There is a tradition of staying awake on the night of Eid al-Fitr in places that are visible, so as to witness the sunrise.
Certainly, there are religious justifications within Christianity for this tradition, but it can well be said that it may have originally been a celebration of spring and fertility prior to Christianity.
Most traditional churches usually hold the Easter Vigil on Saturday night during the Easter holiday, whereas this congregation often celebrates the resurrection of Christ at midnight.
