Due to the great distance from the continent, mammals were unable to reach there, so the giant tortoise is the largest animal that grazes in the Galápagos.
Since humans arrived in the Galápagos, many mammals have been introduced to the islands, including goats, horses, cattle, mice, cats, and dogs.
If you visit the North or South Pole during winter, you will witness the polar night, meaning the sun does not rise above the horizon.
This provides a good opportunity to see the aurora, as the sky will be fairly dark throughout the day.
Since these areas are sparsely populated and, precisely for this reason, do not usually cause light pollution, you can also enjoy the stars.
Japanese work culture is more hierarchical and formal than what Westerners are accustomed to.
The clothes are standard work attire, and colleagues address each other by surname or professional titles.
Collaboration in the workplace is very important, and instead of praising individual achievements, emphasis should be placed on group efforts.
Workers must often obtain the approval of their superiors for every decision they make, and they are expected to obey their superiors' instructions without question.
